window.NEXTSTEP_N2_GRAMMAR={"patterns":[["〜に際して","on the occasion of; when; at the time of","新製品の発売に際して、記者会見が開かれた。","A press conference was held on the occasion of the new product's launch.","Formal; for special, one-off occasions (ceremonies, departures, contracts). Near-synonym of 〜にあたって, which adds a sense of preparing for or facing the event; に際して simply marks the occasion.","विशेष अवसरमा","Noun + に際して / Verb-dict + に際して / Noun + に際しての + Noun","海外へ渡航するに際しては、現地の安全情報を必ず確認してください。","When traveling abroad, be sure to check the local safety information.",["time","formal"],"〜にさいして","契約の更新に際しての注意事項をまとめました。","We have summarized the points to note when renewing the contract."],["〜に伴って","along with; as; accompanying","高齢化に伴って、医療費は年々増加している。","Along with the aging of the population, medical costs are rising year by year.","〜に伴い is the more written form. Like 〜につれて it can describe gradual change, but it also covers one-off events that bring about another (e.g. a relocation).","सँगसँगै परिवर्तन हुँदा","Noun + に伴って / Verb-dict + の + に伴って / Noun + に伴う + Noun","工場の移転に伴い、約二百人の従業員が転勤することになった。","With the relocation of the factory, about two hundred employees are to be transferred.",["change","simultaneity","formal"],"〜にともなって","台風の接近に伴う大雨に注意してください。","Please watch out for heavy rain accompanying the approaching typhoon."],["〜に応じて","according to; depending on; in response to","この奨学金は、家庭の収入に応じて支給額が変わる。","The amount of this scholarship varies according to household income.","B is adjusted to match A (ability, budget, season, requests). Compare 〜次第で, which stresses that the outcome is decided entirely by A.","अवस्थाअनुसार वा मागअनुसार","Noun + に応じて / Noun + に応じた + Noun","お客様のご予算に応じたプランをご提案いたします。","We will propose a plan that suits your budget.",["relation","condition"],"〜におうじて","会社は社員の要望に応じて、在宅勤務の制度を導入した。","In response to employees' requests, the company introduced a work-from-home system."],["〜に反して","contrary to; against; in violation of","大方の予想に反して、無名の新人が優勝した。","Contrary to most people's predictions, an unknown newcomer won the championship.","Used with nouns like 予想, 期待, 意思, 規則. With a rule or law as the noun, it means 'in violation of'.","अपेक्षाको विपरीत","Noun + に反して / Noun + に反する + Noun / Noun + に反した + Noun","本人の意思に反して、彼は地方の支店に異動させられた。","Against his own wishes, he was transferred to a regional branch.",["contrast","formal"],"〜にはんして","たとえ上司の指示であっても、法律に反することはすべきではない。","Even if your boss tells you to, you shouldn't do anything that goes against the law."],["〜に基づいて","based on; on the basis of","この映画は実際に起きた事件に基づいて制作された。","This film was made based on an incident that actually happened.","The basis is a firm standard such as data, law, facts or experience, and B follows it closely. Compare 〜をもとに, used for material from which something new is created.","तथ्य वा आधारअनुसार","Noun + に基づいて / Noun + に基づく + Noun / Noun + に基づいた + Noun","アンケートの結果に基づき、来年度の計画を見直すことにした。","Based on the survey results, we decided to revise next year's plan.",["relation","formal"],"〜にもとづいて","科学的な根拠に基づいた判断が求められている。","Decisions grounded in scientific evidence are called for."],["〜にわたって","over; throughout; spanning (a whole period or area)","工事は三か月にわたって行われる予定だ。","The construction is scheduled to take place over three months.","Stresses the full extent of a long period, a wide area or many items (多岐にわたる). Not used for short or small spans.","लामो अवधि वा ठूलो क्षेत्रभर","Noun + にわたって / Noun + にわたる + Noun","昨夜の大雪で、関東地方の広い範囲にわたって交通が乱れた。","Last night's heavy snow disrupted transportation over a wide area of the Kanto region.",["time","range","formal"],"","両国の首脳は、二日間にわたる会談を終えた。","The leaders of the two countries concluded two days of talks."],["〜に沿って","along; in line with; following","川に沿って桜並木が二キロほど続いている。","A row of cherry trees stretches for about two kilometers along the river.","Literal use: along a road, river or coast. Abstract use: following a plan, policy, or someone's wishes.","अनुरूप, मार्ग वा दिशाअनुसार","Noun + に沿って / Noun + に沿った + Noun","マニュアルに沿って作業を進めてください。","Please proceed with the work according to the manual.",["relation","manner"],"〜にそって","お客様のご要望に沿ったデザインを考えます。","We will come up with a design that meets the customer's wishes."],["〜に加えて","in addition to; on top of","今年は猛暑に加えて雨不足が続き、野菜の価格が高騰している。","This year, on top of the extreme heat, there has been a prolonged lack of rain, and vegetable prices have soared.","Somewhat formal; 〜に加え is the written form. The added item is often marked with も.","यसका अतिरिक्त","Noun + に加えて","この仕事には、語学力に加えて交渉力も必要だ。","This job requires negotiating skills in addition to language ability.",["addition","formal"],"〜にくわえて","",""],["〜をめぐって","over; concerning; surrounding (an issue of dispute)","新しい空港の建設をめぐって、住民の意見が二つに分かれている。","Residents are divided over the construction of a new airport.","The verb that follows is about debate, conflict or competition (議論する, 対立する, 争う). Unlike 〜について, it isn't used for simply explaining a topic.","सम्बन्धमा बहस हुँदा","Noun + をめぐって / Noun + をめぐる + Noun","父の遺産をめぐって、兄弟の間でもめごとが起きた。","A dispute broke out between the siblings over their father's inheritance.",["topic","relation"],"","首相の発言をめぐる議論は、今も続いている。","The debate surrounding the prime minister's remarks is still going on."],["〜を通じて / 〜を通して","through; via; by way of; throughout (a period)","共通の友人を通じて、今の妻と知り合った。","I got to know my wife through a mutual friend.","Largely interchangeable. 〜を通して tends to stress a deliberate process or experience; 〜を通じて is a little more formal and common with media, contacts and periods (一年を通じて).","कुनै माध्यमबाट वा सम्पूर्ण अवधिभर","Noun + を通じて / Noun + を通して","ボランティア活動を通して、地域の人々とのつながりが深まった。","Through volunteer work, my ties with people in the community grew stronger.",["means","time"],"〜をつうじて / 〜をとおして","この地域は一年を通じて雨が少ない。","This region gets little rain throughout the year."],["〜をきっかけに","taking the opportunity of; triggered by; with ... as the start","大学時代の留学をきっかけに、国際協力の仕事に興味を持つようになった。","Studying abroad in college got me interested in international cooperation work.","Marks an event that led to a new start or change. The formal equivalent 〜を契機に is common in writing.","कुनै घटनालाई अवसर बनाएर","Noun + をきっかけに / Noun + をきっかけとして / Verb-plain + の + をきっかけに","引っ越したのをきっかけに、家具をすべて買い替えた。","I took the move as a chance to replace all my furniture.",["reason","change"],"","",""],["〜を除いて","except; excluding; apart from","年末年始を除いて、図書館は毎日開いている。","The library is open every day except during the New Year holidays.","More formal than 〜以外. 〜を除き is the written form.","बाहेक","Noun + を除いて / Noun + を除き / Noun + を除く + Noun","一部の地域を除き、明日は全国的に晴れるでしょう。","Except for some areas, it will be sunny nationwide tomorrow.",["exclusion","formal"],"〜をのぞいて","この件について知っているのは、私を除いて三人しかいない。","Apart from me, only three people know about this."],["〜かのようだ","as if; as though (when it isn't really so)","彼はまるで何も知らないかのような顔をしていた。","He wore a look as if he knew nothing at all.","More literary than 〜ようだ and clearly signals that the comparison is not literally true. Often paired with まるで. Also 〜かのように / 〜かのような.","मानौँ त्यस्तै भएजस्तो देखिनु","Verb-plain / i-Adj + かのようだ / na-Adj + である + かのようだ / Noun + である + かのようだ","三月なのに、真冬に戻ったかのような寒さだ。","It's March, yet it's so cold it feels as if we'd gone back to midwinter.",["appearance","written"],"","その記者は、うわさをまるで事実であるかのように報じた。","The reporter reported the rumor as though it were fact."],["〜かねない","could well; might (lead to something bad)","そんな無理な運転をしていたら、大事故を起こしかねない。","If you keep driving that recklessly, you could end up causing a serious accident.","Only for undesirable outcomes. Despite the ない, the meaning is positive: 'there's a real risk that ...'. Don't confuse with 〜かねる (cannot).","नराम्रो नतिजा हुन पनि सक्छ","Verb-stem + かねない","不用意な一言が、会社の信用を失うことにつながりかねない。","A careless remark could end up costing the company its credibility.",["possibility","conjecture"],"","あの人なら、平気でうそをつきかねない。","He's just the kind of person who might lie without batting an eye."],["〜かねる","cannot; be unable to (polite refusal); find it hard to","申し訳ございませんが、そのご質問にはお答えしかねます。","I'm very sorry, but I'm unable to answer that question.","A soft, formal way to decline, very common in customer service. It expresses reluctance or difficulty for the speaker, not physical inability.","विनम्र रूपमा गर्न नसक्नु","Verb-stem + かねる","個人情報に関するお問い合わせには、お電話では対応いたしかねます。","We are unable to respond to inquiries about personal information by phone.",["ability","politeness","formal"],"","彼のやり方には、どうしても賛成しかねる。","I just can't bring myself to agree with his methods."],["〜ずにはいられない","can't help doing; can't resist doing","あまりにひどいニュースに、怒りを感じずにはいられなかった。","I couldn't help feeling angry at such terrible news.","する becomes せずにはいられない. 〜ないではいられない is a slightly more conversational equivalent. An inner urge, unlike 〜ざるを得ない (forced by circumstances).","नगरी बस्न नसक्नु","Verb-nai stem + ずにはいられない","彼女の苦労話を聞いて、泣かずにはいられなかった。","Hearing about the hardships she'd been through, I couldn't help crying.",["emotion","emphasis"],"","このシリーズは、一度読み始めたら最後まで読まずにはいられない。","Once you start this series, you can't stop until you've read it to the end."],["〜ざるを得ない","have no choice but to; cannot help but","予算が足りないので、計画を縮小せざるを得ない。","The budget is insufficient, so we have no choice but to scale back the plan.","Circumstances force an action the speaker doesn't really want to take. する becomes せざるを得ない. More formal than 〜しかない.","गर्नैपर्ने बाध्यता हुनु","Verb-nai stem + ざるを得ない","上司の命令だったので、気が進まなくても行かざるを得なかった。","It was my boss's order, so I had to go even though I didn't feel like it.",["obligation","formal"],"〜ざるをえない","彼の努力だけは認めざるを得ない。","I have to admit, at least, that he made an effort."],["〜てはいられない","can't afford to (keep) doing; can't just","締め切りが迫っているので、のんびりしてはいられない。","The deadline is approaching, so I can't afford to take it easy.","The situation doesn't allow one to stay in state A, so one feels pushed to act. Casual: 〜ちゃいられない / 〜てらんない.","यस्तो गरिरहन सकिँदैन; तुरुन्त केही गर्नुपर्ने अवस्था","Verb-te + はいられない","困っている人を見ると、黙ってはいられない性格だ。","I'm the type who can't stay quiet when I see someone in trouble.",["negation","necessity"],"","",""],["〜ものか","no way (will I); as if; I'll never","あんな失礼な店には、二度と行くものか。","No way am I ever going to that rude shop again.","Strong emotional denial or refusal; not a real question. Conversational form: 〜もんか; polite/feminine: 〜ものですか.","कुनै हालतमा गर्ने छैन वा हुनै सक्दैन","Verb-dict / i-Adj / na-Adj + な + ものか","一度や二度失敗したくらいで、諦めるもんか。","As if I'd give up just because I failed once or twice.",["negation","emphasis","emotion"],"","あの人の気持ちなんて、君に分かるものか。","As if you could understand how she feels."],["〜ものの","although; even though (but the expected result doesn't follow)","免許は取ったものの、怖くてまだ一度も運転していない。","Although I got my license, I'm too scared and still haven't driven once.","Admits the first fact, then says things didn't go as it would suggest. More written than 〜けれども.","भए तापनि","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + ものの","新しい制度は導入されたものの、十分に活用されていないのが現状だ。","Although the new system has been introduced, the reality is that it isn't being fully used.",["concession","written"],"","この部屋は駅から近いものの、日当たりが悪いのが難点だ。","This apartment is close to the station, but its drawback is that it gets little sunlight."],["〜ものなら","if (it were possible); if only one could","できるものなら、学生時代に戻ってもう一度やり直したい。","If only I could, I'd go back to my student days and do it all over again.","For something hard or impossible to do; the main clause is often 〜たい or a challenge. Don't confuse with N1 〜(よ)うものなら ('if one dared to ..., something bad would happen').","सम्भव भए त; यस्तो गर्न सके","Verb-dict (potential form) + ものなら","行けるものなら行きたいが、その日はどうしても仕事を休めない。","I'd go if I could, but I just can't take that day off work.",["condition","wish"],"","止められるものなら止めてみろ。","Stop me if you can."],["〜くらいなら / 〜ぐらいなら","rather than; if it comes to (doing that), I'd rather","あんな人に頭を下げるくらいなら、会社を辞めたほうがましだ。","I'd rather quit my job than bow my head to someone like him.","A is something the speaker strongly dislikes; B is the lesser evil or better choice, often with 〜ほうがいい / 〜ほうがましだ.","त्यो गर्नुको सट्टा यो गर्नु राम्रो","Verb-dict + くらいなら / Verb-dict + ぐらいなら","途中で投げ出すぐらいなら、最初から引き受けないほうがいい。","If you're going to give up halfway, it's better not to take it on in the first place.",["comparison","condition"],"","",""],["〜ものがある","there is something (about it that is) ...; it really is","この画家の初期の作品には、見る人の心を強く打つものがある。","There is something in this painter's early works that deeply moves the viewer.","Expresses the speaker's strong impression of a quality sensed in something. It's an evaluation, not a statement about literal existence.","महसुस गर्नुपर्ने विशेष गुण वा प्रभाव हुनु","Verb-dict / i-Adj / na-Adj + な + ものがある","毎日二時間かけて通勤するのは、正直つらいものがある。","Honestly, commuting two hours every day is pretty tough.",["emotion","emphasis"],"","若い選手たちの成長ぶりには、目を見張るものがある。","The progress of the young players is truly remarkable."],["〜ことか","how ...!; how much ...!","この日が来るのを、どれほど待ち望んだことか。","How long I've waited for this day to come!","Usually paired with どんなに, どれほど, 何度, etc. Not a real question; it conveys deep feeling. Slightly written or dramatic in tone.","कति धेरै! तीव्र भावना व्यक्त गर्ने","Question word + … + Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な + ことか","一人暮らしを始めて、家族のありがたさを何度感じたことか。","Since I started living alone, I can't count how many times I've felt grateful for my family.",["exclamation","emotion","emphasis"],"","無事だと聞いて、どんなに安心したことか。","What a relief it was to hear you were safe!"],["〜ことに（は）","(emotion)-ly; what is (surprising, sad, etc.) is that","驚いたことに、彼は会社を辞めてパン屋を開いたそうだ。","Surprisingly, I heard he quit his company and opened a bakery.","An emotion word (驚いた, 残念な, うれしい, 不思議な) states the speaker's feeling before giving the fact. Fairly written.","आश्चर्य वा दुःखको कुरा के हो भने","Verb-ta / i-Adj / na-Adj + な + ことに（は）","残念なことに、その美しい建物は来月取り壊されることになった。","Sadly, it has been decided that the beautiful building will be torn down next month.",["emotion","written"],"","うれしいことには、応募作品が予想の倍以上も集まった。","To our delight, we received more than twice as many entries as expected."],["〜ことだから","knowing (someone); since it's (someone), surely","几帳面な彼のことだから、書類はもう準備してあるだろう。","Knowing how meticulous he is, he's probably got the documents ready already.","From what the speaker knows of a person's character, it leads to a guess about their behavior. Usually followed by だろう, きっと or に違いない.","व्यक्तिको स्वभावका कारण अनुमान गर्दा","Noun + の + ことだから","あの子のことだから、きっとどこかで寄り道をしているんだよ。","Knowing that kid, I bet they've stopped off somewhere on the way.",["reason","conjecture"],"","",""],["〜ことなく","without (doing); without ever","彼は三十年間、一日も休むことなく店を開け続けた。","For thirty years, he kept his shop open without taking a single day off.","A written equivalent of 〜ないで / 〜ずに, often implying that something one might expect to happen did not.","काम नगरीकन","Verb-dict + ことなく","失敗を恐れることなく、新しいことに挑戦してほしい。","I want you to take on new challenges without fearing failure.",["negation","manner","written"],"","",""],["〜ことから","from the fact that; because; judging from","この坂は、昔から桜の名所であることから「桜坂」と呼ばれている。","This slope is called 'Sakura-zaka' because it has long been a famous spot for cherry blossoms.","Gives the evidence or origin behind a name, judgment or conclusion. Common in explanations of place names and in reports.","त्यो तथ्यका कारण वा त्यसबाट थाहा भएर","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + ことから","現場に靴の跡が残っていたことから、犯人は外から侵入したと考えられる。","Given the footprints left at the scene, the culprit is thought to have entered from outside.",["reason","written"],"","",""],["〜ないことには","unless; if ... not (then it can't happen)","実際に会って話してみないことには、どんな人か分からない。","You can't tell what someone is like unless you actually meet and talk to them.","The main clause is negative (分からない, できない, 始まらない): without A, B can't happen. More emphatic than 〜なければ.","नगरेसम्म सम्भव हुँदैन","Verb-nai / i-Adj-ku + ない / na-Adj + でない / Noun + でない + ことには","社長の許可が出ないことには、このプロジェクトは始められない。","We can't start this project unless the president gives permission.",["condition","negation"],"","",""],["〜ことは〜が","it's true that ..., but; (I) do ..., but","あの映画、見たことは見たけど、途中で寝てしまった。","I did watch that movie, but I fell asleep halfway through.","The same word is repeated to admit something only partly before adding a reservation. けど replaces が in speech.","त्यसो त हो, तर अर्को पक्ष पनि छ","Verb-plain + ことは + Verb-plain + が / i-Adj + ことは + i-Adj + が / na-Adj + な + ことは + na-Adj + だ + が","この部屋は広いことは広いが、駅からかなり遠い。","This apartment is spacious, sure, but it's quite far from the station.",["concession","emphasis"],"","彼の説明は、分かることは分かるが、納得はできない。","I do understand his explanation, but I'm not convinced."],["〜あげく","after (a long, troublesome process); in the end","さんざん迷ったあげく、結局どちらも買わなかった。","After agonizing over it for ages, in the end I didn't buy either.","The result is usually negative or disappointing. 〜末(に) is neutral and can end well; あげく stresses frustration. あげくの果てに is an intensified form.","लामो प्रयासपछि अन्ततः (प्रायः अप्रिय नतिजा)","Verb-ta + あげく / Noun + の + あげく","長時間の話し合いのあげく、計画は白紙に戻された。","After hours of discussion, the plan was scrapped altogether.",["result","sequence"],"","彼は無理を重ねたあげく、体を壊して入院してしまった。","After pushing himself too hard for too long, he ruined his health and ended up in the hospital."],["〜あまり（に）","so much that; out of excessive; because of too much","彼女は緊張のあまり、スピーチの内容を忘れてしまった。","She was so nervous that she forgot what she was going to say in her speech.","An extreme degree of a feeling or state leads to an unusual, often unwanted result. Mostly with emotion nouns (緊張, 心配, 驚き, 悲しみ).","अत्यधिक भाव वा अवस्थाका कारण","Verb-dict / Verb-ta / na-Adj + な / Noun + の + あまり（に）","子どもの将来を心配するあまり、親が口を出しすぎることがある。","Out of excessive worry for their children's future, parents sometimes interfere too much.",["degree","result","emotion"],"","うれしさのあまり、思わず涙が出た。","I was so happy that tears came to my eyes."],["〜上（に）","besides; on top of; in addition to","あのレストランは料理がおいしい上に、値段も手頃だ。","That restaurant has delicious food, and on top of that, the prices are reasonable.","Adds a second point of the same kind (good + good, bad + bad). に may be dropped in writing. It isn't normally followed by a command or request.","त्यति मात्र होइन, थप रूपमा","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / Noun + である + 上（に）","道に迷った上に、雨まで降ってきた。","Not only did we get lost, it started raining too.",["addition"],"〜うえ（に）","彼女は仕事が速い上、ミスもほとんどない。","She works fast, and she hardly makes any mistakes either."],["〜上で","after (doing), upon; in (doing), when it comes to","家族とよく相談した上で、お返事いたします。","I'll give you my answer after discussing it carefully with my family.","Verb-ta + 上で: do A first, then B on that basis. Verb-dict + 上で: 'in the process of / for the purpose of A'. Business writing often shortens it to ご確認の上.","काम गरेपछि; काम गर्ने क्रममा विचार गर्दा","Verb-ta + 上で / Noun + の + 上で / Verb-dict + 上で","内容を確認した上で、契約書に署名してください。","Please sign the contract after checking its contents.",["sequence","standpoint"],"〜うえで","外国語を学ぶ上で大切なのは、間違いを恐れないことだ。","What's important in learning a foreign language is not being afraid of mistakes."],["〜以上（は）","since; now that; as long as","引き受けた以上は、最後まで責任を持ってやり遂げるつもりだ。","Now that I've taken it on, I intend to see it through responsibly to the end.","From a given situation, draws an obligation, resolve or firm judgment. Near-synonym of 〜からには; 以上は sounds more formal and logical, からには more like personal resolve.","एकपटक निर्णय वा स्थिति भएपछि जिम्मेवारी लिनु","Verb-plain / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + 以上（は）","プロである以上、言い訳は許されない。","As long as you're a professional, excuses aren't acceptable.",["reason","obligation"],"〜いじょう（は）","証拠がない以上、彼を犯人と決めつけることはできない。","Since there's no evidence, we can't conclude that he's the culprit."],["〜からには","now that; since (having done/being ..., one must)","オリンピックに出るからには、メダルを狙いたい。","Since I'm competing in the Olympics, I want to go for a medal.","Expresses resolve: having reached this situation, one should see it through. Often ends with 〜たい, 〜つもりだ, 〜なければならない. Compare 〜以上(は), which is more formal and neutral.","एकपटक निर्णय गरिसकेपछि जिम्मेवारी लिनु","Verb-plain / Noun + である + からには","自分で決めたからには、途中で投げ出すわけにはいかない。","Since I decided on this myself, I can't just give up halfway.",["reason","intention"],"","",""],["〜からこそ","precisely because; it is because ... that","君のことを思っているからこそ、厳しいことを言うんだ。","It's precisely because I care about you that I'm being hard on you.","Stresses that this reason, and no other, is the real one, often a reason the listener wouldn't expect. Frequently ends with 〜のだ.","ठ्याक्कै त्यही कारणले","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + だ / Noun + だ + からこそ","苦しい時期があったからこそ、今の成功があるのだと思う。","I think it's precisely because we went through hard times that we're successful now.",["reason","emphasis"],"","小さな会社だからこそできるサービスもある。","There are some services we can offer precisely because we're a small company."],["〜からして","judging from; (starting) even with; to begin with","空の様子からして、午後は雨になりそうだ。","Judging from the look of the sky, it's likely to rain in the afternoon.","Two uses: 'judging from X' (basis for a guess), and 'even X, let alone the rest', where one example stands for the whole, often critically.","सामान्य गुण पनि एउटा संकेतबाट देखिनु","Noun + からして","あの店は、店員の態度からして感じが悪い。","That shop is unpleasant, starting with the staff's attitude.",["standpoint","emphasis"],"","彼の話は、最初の前提からして間違っている。","His argument is wrong right from its first premise."],["〜からすると / 〜からすれば","judging from; from the standpoint of","あの話し方からすると、彼は関西の出身だろう。","Judging from the way he talks, he's probably from the Kansai area.","Gives either the evidence for a judgment or the viewpoint of a person. Close to 〜から見ると; unlike 〜からいうと, it can take a person.","बाट अनुमान गर्दा वा त्यही दृष्टिकोणबाट","Noun + からすると / Noun + からすれば","親からすれば、子どもはいくつになっても子どもだ。","From a parent's point of view, children are children no matter how old they get.",["standpoint","conjecture"],"","",""],["〜から見ると / 〜から見れば","from the point of view of; judging from; seen from","外国人から見ると、日本の習慣には不思議なものが多いらしい。","Apparently, from a foreigner's point of view, many Japanese customs seem strange.","Looks at something from a person's position or from given evidence. 〜から見て and 〜から見ても are also common.","दृष्टिकोणबाट हेर्दा","Noun + から見ると / Noun + から見れば","今の成績から見れば、第一志望の合格は十分可能だ。","Judging from your current grades, getting into your first-choice school is quite possible.",["standpoint"],"〜からみると / 〜からみれば","",""],["〜からいうと / 〜からいって","in terms of; from the standpoint of; judging by","立地からいうと、駅前のマンションのほうが便利だ。","In terms of location, the apartment in front of the station is more convenient.","The noun is a criterion or viewpoint (立場, 経験, 値段), not a person: say 親からすると, not ×親からいうと. 〜からいえば is also used.","को दृष्टिले वा आधारमा भन्दा","Noun + からいうと / Noun + からいって","これまでの経験からいって、この計画はうまくいかないと思う。","Judging from past experience, I don't think this plan will work.",["standpoint"],"","",""],["〜際（に）","when; at the time of; on the occasion of","お降りの際は、お忘れ物のないようご注意ください。","When getting off, please make sure you don't leave anything behind.","A formal version of 〜とき, common in announcements and instructions. Unlike 〜に際して, it's fine for everyday occasions.","त्यस अवसरमा वा समयमा","Verb-dict / Verb-ta / Noun + の + 際（に）","以前京都を訪れた際に、この寺にも立ち寄った。","When I visited Kyoto before, I also stopped by this temple.",["time","formal"],"〜さい（に）","パスポートを申請する際には、写真と本人確認書類が必要です。","When you apply for a passport, you need a photo and proof of identity."],["〜次第","as soon as (then immediately)","詳しい日程が決まり次第、皆様にご連絡いたします。","We will contact everyone as soon as the detailed schedule is decided.","Formal, for a planned future action that follows right after A (contacting, starting). Not used when the main clause is in the past. Compare 〜次第で (depending on).","काम पूरा हुनेबित्तिकै","Verb-stem + 次第 / Noun + 次第","資料が届き次第、内容を確認してお返事します。","As soon as the materials arrive, I'll check them and get back to you.",["time","sequence","formal"],"〜しだい","定員になり次第、受付を締め切らせていただきます。","Registration will close as soon as capacity is reached."],["〜次第だ / 〜次第で","depending on; it depends on","合格できるかどうかは、これからの努力次第だ。","Whether you pass depends on your efforts from now on.","The outcome is decided by A. 〜次第では points to one possible outcome among several.","नतिजा कुनै अवस्था वा निर्णयमा निर्भर हुनु","Noun + 次第だ / Noun + 次第で / Noun + 次第では","天気次第で、明日の予定を変えるかもしれない。","Depending on the weather, we may change tomorrow's plans.",["condition","relation"],"〜しだいだ / 〜しだいで","考え方次第では、失敗も貴重な経験になる。","Depending on how you look at it, even failure can be a valuable experience."],["〜末（に）","after (a long process of); finally, at the end of","半年にわたる交渉の末、両社はようやく合意に達した。","After six months of negotiations, the two companies finally reached an agreement.","Neutral: the outcome may be good or bad and is often a decision or conclusion. Use 〜あげく when the result is negative or frustrating.","लामो प्रक्रियाको अन्त्यमा","Verb-ta + 末（に） / Noun + の + 末（に）","散々悩んだ末に、彼は留学をあきらめることにした。","After much agonizing, he decided to give up studying abroad.",["result","sequence","written"],"〜すえ（に）","試行錯誤の末に完成したのが、この新しいエンジンだ。","What we finally completed after much trial and error is this new engine."],["〜たところで","even if (it would be no use); no matter how much","今から急いだところで、終電には間に合わないだろう。","Even if we hurry now, we probably won't make the last train.","The main clause says the effort is useless or the result wouldn't matter much. Often with いくら, どんなに, 今さら. Different from 〜たところ (when I did, I found).","गरे पनि नतिजा परिवर्तन नहुनु","Verb-ta + ところで","いくら説明したところで、あの人は聞く耳を持たない。","No matter how much you explain, he just won't listen.",["concession","condition"],"","失敗したところで、失うものは何もない。","Even if we fail, we have nothing to lose."],["〜たところ","when (I) did ..., (I found that); upon doing","駅の窓口で問い合わせたところ、その電車は運休しているとのことだった。","When I asked at the station window, I was told that the train wasn't running.","Reports what turned out after an action, often a discovery. The result is a past fact beyond the speaker's control. More formal than 〜たら.","गरेपछि थाहा भयो कि","Verb-ta + ところ","試しに新しい肥料を使ってみたところ、トマトがよく育った。","When I tried using a new fertilizer, the tomatoes grew very well.",["sequence","result"],"","",""],["〜ばかりか","not only ... but also","彼は約束の時間に遅れたばかりか、謝りもしなかった。","Not only was he late, he didn't even apologize.","Stronger than 〜だけでなく; the second item is often more surprising and marked by も, まで or さえ. Unlike 〜だけでなく, it isn't followed by commands or requests.","मात्र होइन, थप पनि","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / Noun + ばかりか","この薬は効果がないばかりか、副作用まであるそうだ。","I hear this medicine not only doesn't work but even has side effects.",["addition","emphasis"],"","その歌手は国内ばかりか、アジア各国でも人気がある。","That singer is popular not only in Japan but all over Asia."],["〜ばかりに","simply because; just because (with a bad result)","確認を一つ怠ったばかりに、大きな損害を出してしまった。","Simply because I skipped one check, I ended up causing heavy losses.","The main clause is an unwanted result, often with regret. The set form 〜たいばかりに ('just because one wanted to') explains a strong motive.","त्यही कारणले दुर्भाग्यवश","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + ばかりに","正直に話したばかりに、かえって彼女を傷つけてしまった。","Just because I told the truth, I ended up hurting her instead.",["reason","regret","result"],"","英語ができないばかりに、せっかくのチャンスを逃した。","Just because I can't speak English, I missed a great opportunity."],["〜ばかりだ","keep (getting worse); only continue to","駅前の商店街は、客が減るばかりだ。","The shopping street in front of the station just keeps losing customers.","Change continuing in one direction, almost always for the worse. 〜一方だ (N3) is similar but can also describe neutral or good trends.","दिनदिनै एउटै दिशामा परिवर्तन हुनु","Verb-dict + ばかりだ","薬を飲んでいるのに、症状は悪くなるばかりだ。","Even though I'm taking medicine, my symptoms just keep getting worse.",["change","tendency"],"","",""],["〜はもちろん / 〜はもとより","not to mention; of course ... and also","この公園は、週末はもちろん平日も家族連れでにぎわう。","This park is busy with families on weekdays, not to mention weekends.","A is the obvious case; B is added with も or まで. 〜はもとより is more formal and written than 〜はもちろん.","यति त पक्कै, त्यसमाथि अर्को कुरा पनि","Noun + はもちろん / Noun + はもとより","この料理教室では、基本の調理法はもとより、盛り付けのコツまで教えてもらえる。","At this cooking class, they teach you not only basic techniques but even tips on presentation.",["addition","emphasis"],"","地震の後、電気はもちろん、水道もガスも止まってしまった。","After the earthquake, the water and gas were cut off, not to mention the electricity."],["〜はともかく","setting aside; regardless of; whatever about","見た目はともかく、味はなかなかいい。","Looks aside, it tastes pretty good.","Sets A aside to focus on B, which the speaker sees as more important. Compare 〜はさておき, used more to shelve a topic for now and move on.","एक विषय अलग राख्दा","Noun + はともかく / Noun + はともかくとして","結果はともかくとして、最後まで諦めなかったことは評価したい。","Whatever the result, I want to give you credit for not giving up until the end.",["contrast","topic"],"","",""],["〜はさておき","leaving aside; putting aside (for now)","冗談はさておき、そろそろ本題に入りましょう。","Joking aside, let's get down to business.","Often used to switch to the main point, as in 冗談はさておき or それはさておき. Slightly more formal than 〜はともかく.","एक कुरा केही समयका लागि अलग राखेर","Noun + はさておき","費用の問題はさておき、まずは実現可能かどうかを検討すべきだ。","Setting aside the question of cost, we should first consider whether it's feasible.",["topic","contrast"],"","",""],["〜反面 / 〜半面","on the other hand; while (it is ...)","都会の暮らしは便利な反面、ストレスも多い。","City life is convenient, but on the other hand it's also stressful.","Presents two opposite sides of the same thing. 〜一方で (N3) is broader and can also contrast two different things.","एक पक्षमा यस्तो, अर्कोतिर विपरीत","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + 反面","インターネットは情報を手軽に得られる反面、誤った情報も広まりやすい。","While the internet lets you get information easily, false information also spreads easily.",["contrast"],"〜はんめん / 〜はんめん","彼は仕事には厳しい反面、部下思いの一面もある。","Though he's strict about work, he also has a side that looks out for his staff."],["〜ながら（も）","although; despite; while (contrary to expectation)","狭いながらも、日当たりのいい快適な部屋だ。","Although it's small, it's a comfortable, sunny room.","Not the 'while doing' ながら: the subject is in state A, yet B is true. Set phrases: 残念ながら, 知りながら, 及ばずながら.","भए पनि; हुँदाहुँदै","Verb-stem / Verb-nai / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + ながら（も）","悪いと知りながら、つい嘘をついてしまった。","Even though I knew it was wrong, I ended up telling a lie.",["concession","written"],"","彼女は若いながらも、しっかりした考えを持っている。","Young as she is, she has very sound views."],["〜つつ / 〜つつも","while (doing); although, even while","今年の業績を振り返りつつ、来年の目標を考えたい。","While looking back on this year's results, I'd like to think about next year's goals.","つつ alone is a written 〜ながら (two actions at once). つつも means 'although', typically with verbs of knowing or thinking (思いつつ, 知りつつ).","गर्दैगर्दा वा भए पनि","Verb-stem + つつ / Verb-stem + つつも","体に悪いと分かりつつも、夜更かしがやめられない。","Even though I know it's bad for me, I can't stop staying up late.",["simultaneity","concession","written"],"","早く返事をしなければと思いつつ、もう一週間もたってしまった。","Even as I kept thinking I had to reply soon, a whole week has gone by."],["〜つつある","be in the process of; be gradually (changing)","地球の平均気温は、年々上昇しつつある。","The earth's average temperature is steadily rising year by year.","Written style for change that is underway toward some result. Used with change verbs (増える, 回復する, 変わる), not with simple ongoing actions like 食べる.","बिस्तारै परिवर्तन हुँदै जानु","Verb-stem + つつある","この地域の伝統的な祭りは、若者の減少とともに失われつつある。","This area's traditional festivals are gradually being lost as the young population declines.",["change","written"],"","",""],["〜っぱなし","leaving (something) as is; keep (doing) without a break","部屋の電気をつけっぱなしにして出かけてしまった。","I went out and left the light on in my room.","Either something left undone that should have been dealt with (often a complaint), or a state that goes on without a break. Conversational.","काम गरेकै अवस्थामा छोड्नु वा रोकिएन","Verb-stem + っぱなし","今日は朝から立ちっぱなしで、足が痛い。","I've been on my feet since this morning, and my legs hurt.",["state","criticism","casual"],"","窓を開けっぱなしにしないでください。","Please don't leave the window open."],["〜抜く","do to the very end; see through; do thoroughly","足を痛めていたが、彼は最後まで走り抜いた。","Although he had hurt his leg, he ran all the way to the finish.","Stresses finishing something hard despite difficulty, or doing it to the fullest (考え抜く, 生き抜く).","अन्त्यसम्म दृढतापूर्वक पूरा गर्नु","Verb-stem + 抜く","悩み抜いた末に出した結論なので、後悔はない。","It's a conclusion I reached after thinking it through thoroughly, so I have no regrets.",["completion","emphasis"],"〜ぬく","チームは苦しい試合で一点のリードを守り抜いた。","The team held on to its one-point lead through a tough game."],["〜得る / 〜得ない","can; be possible / cannot; be impossible","どんなに注意していても、事故は起こり得る。","No matter how careful you are, accidents can happen.","Logical possibility, not personal skill (not ×泳ぎ得る for 'can swim'). The positive is read うる or える; other forms use え- (えない, えた).","हुन सक्नु वा हुन नसक्नु","Verb-stem + 得る / Verb-stem + 得ない","あの真面目な彼が犯人だなんて、あり得ない。","There's no way someone as serious as him could be the culprit.",["possibility","written"],"〜うる / 〜えない","今回の調査で、これまで知り得なかった事実が明らかになった。","This investigation brought to light facts we had been unable to learn until now."],["〜がたい","hard to; almost impossible to (emotionally)","あの誠実な人が不正をしたとは、信じがたい。","It's hard to believe that such an honest person committed fraud.","Used with verbs of thinking and feeling (信じる, 理解する, 許す, 離れる). Unlike 〜にくい, not for physical difficulty (×この肉は食べがたい).","गर्न वा विश्वास गर्न निकै कठिन","Verb-stem + がたい","彼の失礼な態度は、どうにも許しがたい。","His rude attitude is simply unforgivable.",["possibility","emotion","written"],"","生まれ育った町は、やはり離れがたいものだ。","The town you grew up in is, after all, hard to leave."],["〜ようがない","there's no way to; cannot possibly (no means available)","連絡先が分からないので、知らせようがない。","I don't have his contact details, so there's no way to let him know.","There's no method at all, even if one wanted to. 〜ようもない is more emphatic. With suru-nouns: 説明のしようがない.","गर्ने उपाय छैन","Verb-stem + ようがない / Noun + の + しようがない","これだけ証拠がそろっていては、言い訳のしようがない。","With this much evidence, there's no way to make excuses.",["possibility","negation","means"],"","壊れた部品がもう生産されていないので、直しようがない。","The broken part is no longer made, so there's no way to fix it."],["〜ようでは","if (you are like this / keep doing this), (it's no good)","こんな簡単なミスをするようでは、大きな仕事は任せられない。","If you make simple mistakes like this, we can't trust you with big jobs.","Criticizes an undesirable state and predicts a bad outcome; the main clause is negative (〜ない, 困る, だめだ).","यस्तै अवस्था भएमा","Verb-plain + ようでは","毎朝遅刻しているようでは、信頼を得られないよ。","If you're late every morning, you won't earn anyone's trust.",["condition","criticism"],"","",""],["〜てならない","can't help (feeling); feel terribly; extremely","故郷の母のことが心配でならない。","I can't stop worrying about my mother back home.","For feelings or impressions that arise on their own (気がする, 思われる, 心配だ, 残念だ). More formal and written than 〜てたまらない / 〜てしょうがない.","भावनालाई रोक्न नसक्नु","Verb-te + ならない / i-Adj-ku + てならない / na-Adj + でならない","あのとき本当のことを言わなかったのが、悔やまれてならない。","I bitterly regret not telling the truth back then.",["emotion","degree"],"","この計画には何か裏があるような気がしてならない。","I can't shake the feeling that there's something behind this plan."],["〜てこそ","only by (doing); only when","自分で経験してこそ、本当の意味で理解できるのだ。","Only by experiencing it yourself can you truly understand it.","Stresses that A is the essential condition for the real value or result in B. 〜てはじめて (N3) is more neutral, focusing on timing.","त्यसो गरेपछि मात्र वास्तविक परिणाम आउनु","Verb-te + こそ","お互いに協力し合ってこそ、チームは強くなる。","A team only becomes strong when its members work together.",["condition","emphasis"],"","",""],["〜てからでないと","not until (after doing); only after","実物を見てからでないと、買うかどうか決められない。","I can't decide whether to buy it until I've seen the real thing.","The main clause is negative or expresses difficulty: B can't happen unless A is done first.","त्यो काम नगरुन्जेल अर्को काम सम्भव नहुनु","Verb-te + からでないと / Verb-te + からでなければ","この薬は、医師に相談してからでなければ服用しないでください。","Please do not take this medicine until you have consulted a doctor.",["condition","sequence"],"","",""],["〜て以来","ever since","大学を卒業して以来、彼とは一度も会っていない。","I haven't seen him once since we graduated from university.","The main clause is a state or habit continuing from that past point up to now, not a single later event. More formal than 〜てから.","त्यसबेलादेखि अहिलेसम्म","Verb-te + 以来 / Noun + 以来","この町に越してきて以来、毎朝川沿いを散歩するのが日課になっている。","Ever since I moved to this town, a morning walk along the river has been part of my routine.",["time"],"〜ていらい","創業以来、この店は同じ味を守り続けている。","Since its founding, this shop has kept the same flavor."],["〜に過ぎない","merely; nothing more than; only","それは単なるうわさに過ぎない。","That's nothing more than a rumor.","Downplays something as small or unimportant. Often with ただ or 単なる.","केवल त्यति मात्रै हुनु","Verb-plain / Noun + に過ぎない","私は自分の仕事をしたに過ぎません。","I was merely doing my job.",["limitation","emphasis","formal"],"〜にすぎない","今回明らかになった問題は、氷山の一角に過ぎない。","The problem that has come to light this time is merely the tip of the iceberg."],["〜に限る","nothing beats; the best thing is","疲れたときは、早く寝るに限る。","When you're tired, there's nothing better than going to bed early.","The speaker's personal conviction that something is the best choice; conversational. For a more general 'it's best to', use 〜に越したことはない.","त्यही सबैभन्दा राम्रो विकल्प हुनु","Verb-dict / Verb-nai / Noun + に限る","夏の暑い日は、冷たいビールに限る。","On a hot summer day, nothing beats a cold beer.",["advice","suggestion"],"〜にかぎる","面倒なことには関わらないに限る。","It's best to stay out of troublesome matters."],["〜に限らず","not only; not limited to","この遊園地は、子どもに限らず大人にも人気がある。","This amusement park is popular not only with children but with adults as well.","Widens the scope beyond A; the second part usually has も. Close to 〜だけでなく but a bit more formal.","मात्र नभई अरू पनि","Noun + に限らず","日本に限らず、多くの先進国が少子化の問題を抱えている。","Not just Japan but many developed countries face a falling birthrate.",["range","addition"],"〜にかぎらず","",""],["〜に限って","of all (times/people); precisely when; (someone) of all people wouldn't","傘を持っていない日に限って、雨が降るんだよね。","It always rains on exactly the days I don't have an umbrella.","Two uses: (1) 'just when', complaining that bad luck strikes at the worst time; (2) with はずがない / ない, firm trust that a particular person wouldn't do something.","विशेषगरी त्यही अवस्थामा","Noun + に限って","急いでいるときに限って、電車が遅れる。","The train is always late precisely when I'm in a hurry.",["limitation","emphasis"],"〜にかぎって","うちの子に限って、そんなことをするはずがない。","My child, of all people, would never do such a thing."],["〜に限り","limited to; only (for)","本日ご来店のお客様に限り、全商品を二割引きいたします。","For customers visiting today only, all items are 20% off.","Formal; typical of notices, ads and rules to state who or what a condition applies to.","यही समूह वा समयमा मात्र सीमित","Noun + に限り","先着百名様に限り、記念品を差し上げます。","Commemorative gifts will be given to the first hundred people only.",["limitation","formal"],"〜にかぎり","この駐車場は、住民に限り無料で利用できる。","Parking here is free for residents only."],["〜かぎり","as long as; as far as (to the limit of)","私の知るかぎり、彼が約束を破ったことは一度もない。","As far as I know, he has never once broken a promise.","'As long as' a condition holds, or 'as far as' the limit of knowledge or ability (私の知るかぎり, できるかぎり). Also written 限り. Different from 〜に限り (limited to).","जबसम्म वा ज्ञान/सीमाको हदसम्म","Verb-dict / Verb-te + いる / i-Adj / na-Adj + である / Noun + である + かぎり","体が動くかぎり、この仕事を続けたい。","As long as my body keeps working, I want to continue this job.",["condition","limitation","range"],"","できるかぎりのことはやったので、結果がどうなっても悔いはない。","I did everything I could, so whatever the result, I have no regrets."],["〜ないかぎり","unless; as long as ... not","よほどのことがないかぎり、明日の会議には出席します。","Unless something serious comes up, I'll attend tomorrow's meeting.","B holds as long as A doesn't happen. More emphatic and formal than 〜なければ.","नगरेसम्म; त्यस शर्तबिना होइन","Verb-nai + かぎり","本人が反省しないかぎり、同じ問題は何度でも起こるだろう。","Unless he genuinely reflects on it, the same problem will keep happening.",["condition","negation"],"","",""],["〜にかけては","when it comes to; in terms of (skill)","料理の腕にかけては、うちの父は誰にも負けない。","When it comes to cooking, my father is second to none.","Praises someone's ability in a specific field; typically followed by 誰にも負けない, 一番だ, 自信がある.","कुनै विशेष क्षेत्रमा अरूभन्दा राम्रो","Noun + にかけては / Noun + にかけても","彼女は数字の分析にかけては、社内で右に出る者がいない。","When it comes to analyzing numbers, no one in the company can match her.",["topic","ability"],"","",""],["〜にこたえて","in response to; meeting (expectations, requests)","ファンの声援にこたえて、選手たちは手を振った。","The players waved in response to the fans' cheers.","Used with nouns like 期待, 要望, 声援, 要求. Also written 〜に応えて. Compare 〜に応じて, which means adjusting to a condition.","आशा वा अनुरोधको जवाफमा","Noun + にこたえて / Noun + にこたえる + Noun","利用者の要望にこたえて、図書館の開館時間が延長された。","In response to users' requests, the library's opening hours were extended.",["relation","formal"],"","彼は周囲の期待にこたえる結果を出した。","He produced results that lived up to everyone's expectations."],["〜に先立って","prior to; before","新作映画の公開に先立って、完成披露試写会が開かれた。","Prior to the release of the new film, a premiere screening was held.","Formal; for preparations or events that come before an important occasion. 〜に先立ち is the written form.","अगाडि नै","Noun + に先立って / Verb-dict + に先立って / Noun + に先立つ + Noun","試合開始に先立ち、全員で黙とうをささげた。","Before the start of the match, everyone observed a moment of silence.",["time","sequence","formal"],"〜にさきだって","",""],["〜にしろ / 〜にせよ","even if; whether ... or ...; in any case","たとえ冗談にしろ、そんなことを言うべきではない。","Even if it was a joke, you shouldn't say something like that.","Same meaning as 〜にしても (N3) but more formal; にせよ is the most written. The paired form AにしろBにしろ means 'whether A or B'.","जे भए पनि; जस्तो अवस्थामा पनि","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + にしろ・にせよ","参加するにせよしないにせよ、今週中に返事をください。","Whether you take part or not, please reply by the end of this week.",["concession","formal"],"","いずれにせよ、もう一度話し合う必要がある。","In any case, we need to talk it over again."],["〜にすれば / 〜にしたら","from the standpoint of; for (someone), (it would seem)","子どもにすれば、親の小言はうるさいだけなのだろう。","From a child's point of view, parents' nagging is probably just annoying.","Imagines how things feel from another person's position (usually not the speaker's). Unlike 〜にとって, it focuses on that person's feelings or opinion.","को दृष्टिकोणबाट हेर्दा","Noun + にすれば / Noun + にしたら","毎日遅くまで残業させられる社員にしたら、たまったものではない。","For employees made to work late every day, it's unbearable.",["standpoint"],"","",""],["〜に相違ない","without doubt; must be; surely","この筆跡は、父のものに相違ない。","This handwriting is without doubt my father's.","A written, formal equivalent of 〜に違いない (N3). Also seen on forms: 上記の通り相違ありません ('the above is correct').","निस्सन्देह त्यस्तै हो","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + に相違ない","彼の証言が事実なら、事件の背後には別の人物がいるに相違ない。","If his testimony is true, there must be someone else behind the incident.",["conjecture","formal","written"],"〜にそういない","",""],["〜に越したことはない","it's best to; nothing is better than","どんなに健康でも、定期的に検診を受けるに越したことはない。","No matter how healthy you are, it's best to get regular checkups.","States a common-sense preference, often followed by が / けれど and a practical reservation. Compare 〜に限る, which is a more personal choice.","यही गर्नु सबैभन्दा राम्रो","Verb-dict / Verb-nai / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + に越したことはない","旅行の荷物は、軽いに越したことはない。","When you travel, the lighter your luggage, the better.",["advice","suggestion"],"〜にこしたことはない","住まいは駅に近いに越したことはないが、その分家賃が高くなる。","It's best to live near the station, of course, but the rent goes up accordingly."],["〜にほかならない","nothing other than; none other than; precisely","今回の成功は、社員一人ひとりの努力の結果にほかならない。","This success is nothing other than the result of each employee's efforts.","Strongly asserts that this and nothing else is the case. 〜からにほかならない stresses a reason. Formal/written.","अरू केही नभई यही हो","Noun + にほかならない / Verb-plain + から + にほかならない","彼が厳しく指導するのは、選手の才能を信じているからにほかならない。","He coaches strictly precisely because he believes in the athletes' talent.",["emphasis","written"],"","",""],["〜にもかかわらず","despite; in spite of; although","悪天候にもかかわらず、大勢の観客が会場に集まった。","Despite the bad weather, a large crowd gathered at the venue.","A formal counterpart of 〜のに, common in news and writing; stresses that the result goes against what A would lead one to expect. Don't confuse with 〜にかかわらず (regardless of).","हुँदाहुँदै पनि; त्यसको विपरीत","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + である / Noun + にもかかわらず","何度も注意されたにもかかわらず、彼は同じミスを繰り返した。","Despite being warned many times, he repeated the same mistake.",["concession","formal"],"","",""],["〜にあたって","when; at the time of; on the occasion of (starting something important)","新生活を始めるにあたって、必要な物をリストにまとめた。","When starting my new life, I made a list of the things I'd need.","Formal; used when facing an important undertaking, often with a sense of preparation or resolve. 〜に際して is similar but simply marks the occasion. Written form: 〜にあたり.","विशेष अवसरमा वा सुरु गर्दा","Noun + にあたって / Verb-dict + にあたって / Noun + にあたっての + Noun","開会にあたり、主催者を代表して一言ご挨拶申し上げます。","On the occasion of the opening, allow me to say a few words on behalf of the organizers.",["time","formal"],"","論文を書くにあたっては、引用のルールを守らなければならない。","When writing a thesis, you must follow the rules of citation."],["〜において / 〜における","in; at; in the field of (formal)","卒業式は大講堂において行われます。","The graduation ceremony will be held in the main auditorium.","A formal version of で for places, times, fields or situations. Before a noun, the form is 〜における.","औपचारिक सन्दर्भमा स्थान वा क्षेत्रभित्र","Noun + において / Noun + における + Noun","現代社会における家族の役割について考えてみたい。","I'd like to consider the role of the family in modern society.",["range","formal","written"],"","彼女はデザインの分野において高く評価されている。","She is highly regarded in the field of design."],["〜にかかわらず","regardless of; irrespective of","このセミナーは、経験の有無にかかわらず、どなたでも参加できます。","Anyone can join this seminar, regardless of experience.","Used with nouns implying a range or an opposite pair (年齢, 天候, 有無, 男女). Very close to 〜を問わず. Don't confuse with 〜にもかかわらず (despite).","जे भए पनि; वास्ता नगरी","Noun + にかかわらず / Verb-dict + Verb-nai + にかかわらず","天候にかかわらず、試合は予定通り行います。","The match will go ahead as scheduled regardless of the weather.",["concession","range","formal"],"","出席するしないにかかわらず、必ず返信してください。","Please be sure to reply whether or not you will attend."],["〜にかかわる","affecting; concerning (something important); relating to","これは人の命にかかわる問題だから、慎重に判断しなければならない。","This is a matter of life and death, so we must judge carefully.","Used for things with serious consequences: 命, 名誉, 信用, 将来. Also written 〜に関わる.","सम्बन्ध राख्नु वा गम्भीर असर पार्नु","Noun + にかかわる","会社の信用にかかわるようなミスは、絶対に避けたい。","I absolutely want to avoid any mistake that could damage the company's reputation.",["relation"],"","",""],["〜につき","per; for each; due to (in formal notices)","駐車料金は、一時間につき三百円です。","Parking costs 300 yen per hour.","Two separate uses: 'per' with quantities, and 'because of' on notices and signs (工事中につき). The reason use is very formal.","कारणले वा प्रतिको हिसाबले (सूचना)","Noun + につき","本日は定休日につき、お休みさせていただきます。","We are closed today as it is our regular holiday.",["reason","quantity","formal"],"","工事中につき、この先は通行止めです。","Due to construction, the road ahead is closed."],["〜に向けて","toward; aimed at; in preparation for; addressed to","来年の全国大会に向けて、毎日練習に励んでいる。","We're practicing hard every day for next year's national tournament.","Marks a goal or event being worked toward, or the audience something is directed at. Different from 〜向け (N3), 'designed for'.","लक्ष्यतर्फ वा तयारीका लागि","Noun + に向けて / Noun + に向けた + Noun","政府は、温室効果ガス削減に向けた新しい計画を発表した。","The government announced a new plan aimed at reducing greenhouse gases.",["purpose","relation"],"〜にむけて","大統領は国民に向けてメッセージを発表した。","The president issued a message addressed to the nation."],["〜のもとで / 〜のもとに","under (guidance, influence, a rule); with","私は大学院で、有名な教授のもとで研究を続けた。","In graduate school, I continued my research under a famous professor.","Under someone's guidance, protection or influence, or under a rule or condition. Often written 〜の下で / 〜の下に.","को नेतृत्व/परिस्थितिमा","Noun + のもとで / Noun + のもとに","明るい太陽のもとで、子どもたちが元気に遊んでいる。","Children are playing happily under the bright sun.",["relation","state","formal"],"","すべての国民は、法のもとに平等である。","All citizens are equal under the law."],["〜抜きで / 〜抜きに","without; leaving out","今日は仕事の話抜きで、ゆっくり楽しみましょう。","Let's leave work talk out of it today and just relax and enjoy ourselves.","Leaves out something normally included. 〜抜きには〜ない / 〜を抜きにしては〜ない means 'can't ... without'.","बाहेक राखेर; नगरीकन","Noun + 抜きで / Noun + 抜きに / Noun + 抜きの + Noun","彼の協力抜きには、このプロジェクトは成功しなかっただろう。","Without his cooperation, this project probably wouldn't have succeeded.",["exclusion","manner"],"〜ぬきで / 〜ぬきに","朝食抜きで出勤する人が増えている。","More and more people are going to work without breakfast."],["〜をこめて","with (feeling); full of; putting ... into","母の誕生日に、感謝の気持ちをこめて手紙を書いた。","For my mother's birthday, I wrote her a letter full of gratitude.","Used with feelings or intentions (愛, 感謝, 願い, 心). Also written 〜を込めて.","मनको भावना वा मनसाय समेटेर","Noun + をこめて","職人が一つ一つ心をこめて作った器です。","These bowls were made one by one, with great care, by craftsmen.",["emotion","manner"],"","",""],["〜を中心に","centered on; focusing on; mainly","今回の地震では、沿岸部を中心に大きな被害が出た。","In this earthquake, serious damage occurred mainly in coastal areas.","A is the core or main part of a wider area, group or activity.","मुख्य रूपमा केन्द्रित","Noun + を中心に / Noun + を中心として / Noun + を中心とした + Noun","この講座では、会話を中心に実践的な日本語を学びます。","In this course, you'll learn practical Japanese with a focus on conversation.",["range","relation"],"〜をちゅうしんに","若者を中心とした新しいファッションが広がっている。","New fashions popular mainly among young people are spreading."],["〜をもとに","based on; using ... as a basis or source","この小説は、作者自身の体験をもとに書かれている。","This novel is based on the author's own experiences.","A is the material or hint from which something new is made. 〜に基づいて is used when strictly following a rule or fact as a standard.","आधार बनाएर","Noun + をもとに / Noun + をもとにして / Noun + をもとにした + Noun","集めたデータをもとにして、グラフを作成した。","I made a graph based on the data I had collected.",["relation","means"],"","",""],["〜を問わず","regardless of; irrespective of","この仕事は、年齢や経験を問わず応募できます。","Anyone can apply for this job regardless of age or experience.","Used with nouns implying a range or an opposite pair (男女, 昼夜, 国内外). Very close to 〜にかかわらず; を問わず is typical of job ads and notices.","जेसुकै भए पनि","Noun + を問わず","この曲は国内外を問わず、多くの人々に愛されている。","This song is loved by many people both in Japan and abroad.",["range","formal"],"〜をとわず","救急隊員は、昼夜を問わず出動に備えている。","Paramedics are ready to respond day or night."],["〜をはじめ","starting with; including; such as (a representative example)","京都には、金閣寺をはじめ、多くの有名な寺がある。","Kyoto has many famous temples, including Kinkakuji.","Names the most representative member of a group, then refers to the group as a whole. The main clause covers many items, not just A.","लाई उदाहरण मानेर सुरु गर्दै","Noun + をはじめ / Noun + をはじめとして / Noun + をはじめとする + Noun","社長をはじめとして、社員全員がこの計画に賛成した。","Everyone in the company, starting with the president, agreed to this plan.",["example","addition"],"","米をはじめとする農産物の価格が上昇している。","Prices of farm products, rice among them, are rising."],["〜を〜として","treating (A) as (B); with A as B","この大会は、地域の活性化を目的として開かれている。","This event is held with the aim of revitalizing the local area.","Puts A in the role or function of B; common B nouns are 目的, 目標, 中心, 対象, 条件. 〜を〜にして is a more casual variant.","कुनै वस्तु/व्यक्तिलाई निश्चित भूमिकामा राखेर","Noun + を + Noun + として / Noun + を + Noun + とする","私たちのチームは、営業部の山口さんをリーダーとして新しい企画に取り組んでいる。","Our team is working on a new project with Ms. Yamaguchi from sales as leader.",["standpoint","manner"],"","",""],["〜かというと","if you ask whether (actually, not); the reason why ... is","高い料理ならおいしいかというと、必ずしもそうではない。","Is expensive food always delicious? Not necessarily.","With a question word (なぜ, どうして) it introduces an explanation. Without one, it raises a question only to deny the easy assumption (〜かというと、そうではない). Also 〜かといえば.","किन/के हो भनेर सोध्दा भने","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + かというと / Question word + … + かというと","なぜこの仕事を選んだかというと、人の役に立ちたかったからです。","The reason I chose this job is that I wanted to help people.",["question","topic"],"","では、彼の意見に全面的に賛成かというと、そういうわけでもない。","But does that mean I fully agree with his opinion? Not exactly."],["〜かと思ったら / 〜かと思うと","just when; no sooner than; the moment","空が急に暗くなったかと思ったら、激しい雨が降り出した。","No sooner had the sky suddenly gone dark than it started to pour.","B follows A immediately and unexpectedly. It describes what the speaker observes, so it isn't used for the speaker's own actions.","त्यस्तो भयो जस्तो लाग्नासाथ अर्को घटना हुनु","Verb-ta + かと思ったら / Verb-ta + かと思うと","息子は帰ってきたかと思うと、すぐにまた遊びに出かけた。","My son had no sooner come home than he went straight back out to play.",["time","sequence","surprise"],"〜かとおもったら / 〜かとおもうと","やっと静かになったかと思ったら、また隣の工事が始まった。","Just when I thought it had finally gotten quiet, the construction next door started up again."],["〜か〜ないかのうちに","as soon as; barely ... when","ベルが鳴るか鳴らないかのうちに、生徒たちは教室を飛び出した。","The bell had barely rung when the students rushed out of the classroom.","The same verb is repeated in positive and negative: it's unclear whether A has even finished before B happens. Describes observed events.","काम पूरा हुन नपाउँदै अर्को घटना हुनु","Verb-dict + か + Verb-nai + かのうちに / Verb-ta + か + Verb-nai + かのうちに","彼は布団に入ったか入らないかのうちに、いびきをかき始めた。","He had barely gotten into bed when he started snoring.",["time","simultaneity"],"","",""],["〜きり","since (and nothing after); only; just","兄は十年前に家を出たきり、一度も連絡をよこさない。","My brother left home ten years ago and hasn't been in touch once since.","Verb-ta + きり: something happened and the expected follow-up never came (often with ない). Noun + きり: 'only' (一度きり, 二人きり). Casual: 〜っきり.","त्यस समयदेखि; त्यति मात्र","Verb-ta + きり / Noun + きり","今度の休みは、久しぶりに二人きりで旅行したい。","For our next holiday, I'd like us to take a trip, just the two of us, for the first time in ages.",["limitation","time"],"","チャンスは一度きりだから、絶対に失敗できない。","There's only one chance, so I absolutely can't fail."],["〜げ","seeming; looking (as if); with an air of","彼女は窓の外を寂しげに見つめていた。","She was gazing out the window with a lonely look.","Describes a feeling visible in someone's face or manner; conjugates like a na-adjective (〜げな, 〜げに). Rather literary.","त्यस्तो देखिने वा भावना झल्किने","i-Adj stem + げ / na-Adj + げ / Verb-stem + たげ","少年は得意げな顔で、描いた絵を見せてくれた。","The boy proudly showed me the picture he had drawn.",["appearance","emotion","written"],"","何か言いたげな様子だったが、彼は黙って帰っていった。","He looked as if he wanted to say something, but he left without a word."],["〜っこない","no way; there's absolutely no chance","こんな量の仕事、一日で終わりっこないよ。","There's no way this much work will get done in one day.","Casual speech only; often with potential verbs (できっこない, 分かりっこない). A casual equivalent of 〜わけがない.","कुनै हालतमा सम्भव छैन","Verb-stem + っこない","宝くじなんて当たりっこないと思いながら、毎年買っている。","I buy lottery tickets every year, even though I figure there's no way I'll win.",["possibility","negation","casual"],"","",""],["〜どころか","far from; let alone; on the contrary","薬を飲んだが、熱は下がるどころか、ますます高くなった。","I took medicine, but far from going down, my fever got even higher.","Either the reality is the opposite of A, or not even something lesser than A is possible (AどころかBも〜ない).","उल्टै; त्यति मात्र होइन, बिल्कुल विपरीत","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + どころか","忙しくて、旅行どころか週末に休むこともできない。","I'm so busy I can't even take weekends off, let alone travel.",["contrast","emphasis"],"","彼は謝るどころか、逆に私を責めてきた。","Far from apologizing, he turned around and blamed me."],["〜どころではない","this is no time for; out of the question","来週は試験なので、遊びに行くどころではない。","I have exams next week, so this is no time to be going out.","The circumstances make A impossible or unthinkable right now. Casual: 〜どころじゃない.","त्यस्तो गर्ने फुर्सद/अवस्था नै नहुनु","Verb-dict / Noun + どころではない","引っ越しの準備に追われて、花見どころではなかった。","I was so busy getting ready for the move that cherry blossom viewing was out of the question.",["negation","emphasis"],"","",""],["〜とは限らない","not necessarily; not always","値段が高いからといって、品質がいいとは限らない。","Just because something is expensive doesn't necessarily mean it's good quality.","Denies that something is always true; often with 必ずしも or 〜からといって.","सधैँ वा सबै अवस्थामा सही नहुनु","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + とは限らない","専門家の意見がいつも正しいとは限らない。","Experts' opinions are not always right.",["negation","possibility"],"〜とはかぎらない","",""],["〜というものだ","that's what (A) is; that's just how it is; that's really","困っている人がいたら助ける。それが人情というものだ。","When someone's in trouble, you help them. That's what human kindness is.","A firm opinion about what something really is or how things naturally are. Often used to criticize an attitude.","यस्तो नै हो; स्वाभाविक मूल्याङ्कन","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + というものだ","何の準備もせずに合格しようなんて、虫がよすぎるというものだ。","Expecting to pass without any preparation is just wishful thinking.",["emphasis","criticism"],"","一人で全部やろうとするのは無理というものだ。","Trying to do it all alone is simply unrealistic."],["〜というものではない","it's not (necessarily) the case that; it doesn't follow that","練習は長くやればいいというものではない。","Longer practice isn't automatically better practice.","Rejects an oversimplified belief; often with 〜ばいい or 〜さえ〜ば. 〜というものでもない is a softer variant.","त्यो मात्र पर्याप्त वा सही होइन","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + というものではない","お金さえあれば幸せになれるというものではない。","It's not as if money alone can make you happy.",["negation","criticism"],"","",""],["〜といっても","although I say; even though (it's called)","料理ができるといっても、簡単なものしか作れません。","I say I can cook, but I can only make simple things.","Corrects or limits what the listener might assume from the first statement. Often followed by たった, ただ or 〜しか〜ない.","भने पनि वास्तवमा","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj / Noun + といっても","海外に住んでいたといっても、たった半年のことだ。","I did live abroad, but only for six months.",["concession","limitation"],"","",""],["〜といえば / 〜というと","speaking of; when you think of; if you mention","日本の夏の風物詩といえば、やはり花火大会だろう。","When you think of summer traditions in Japan, fireworks festivals come to mind first.","Introduces something closely associated with a topic, or picks up a word just mentioned to shift the conversation. 〜といったら is a more emotional variant.","त्यो विषय आयो भने सम्झिने कुरा","Noun + といえば / Noun + というと","北海道というと、広い大地とおいしい海産物を思い浮かべる人が多い。","When people hear 'Hokkaido', many picture vast open land and delicious seafood.",["topic","example"],"","旅行といえば、来月の出張の件はどうなりましたか。","Speaking of travel, what happened with next month's business trip?"],["〜ほかない","have no choice but to; there's nothing to do but","終電を逃してしまったので、タクシーで帰るほかない。","I've missed the last train, so I have no choice but to take a taxi home.","A somewhat formal equivalent of 〜しかない (N3). Variants: 〜ほかはない, 〜よりほかない, 〜ほかしかたがない.","अर्को उपाय नै छैन","Verb-dict + ほかない / Verb-dict + よりほかない","自分で決めた道なのだから、前に進むよりほかない。","It's the path I chose, so there's nothing to do but keep going.",["obligation","decision"],"","",""],["〜まい","will not (resolve); probably won't (conjecture)","あんな恥ずかしい思いは、二度とするまいと心に誓った。","I swore to myself that I would never go through such embarrassment again.","Written/formal. First person: firm resolve not to (〜ないつもりだ). Others: negative guess (〜ないだろう). する → するまい / すまい. Often 〜まいと思う / 〜まいと決心する.","नगर्ने संकल्प वा सायद नगर्ला","Verb-dict + まい / Verb-stem (ichidan verbs) + まい","この大雨では、今日はもう誰も来るまい。","In this downpour, probably no one else will come today.",["negation","intention","conjecture"],"","",""],["〜（よ）うではないか","let's (formal call to action); why don't we","この町の未来のために、皆で力を合わせようではないか。","For the future of this town, let us all join forces.","A strong, formal appeal to a group, typical of speeches and editorials. The casual version is 〜(よ)うじゃないか.","आउनुहोस्, सँगै गरौँ भन्ने आह्वान","Verb-volitional + ではないか / Verb-volitional + ではありませんか","失敗を恐れず、新しいことに挑戦してみようではありませんか。","Let's not fear failure, and try taking on something new, shall we?",["invitation","formal"],"","",""],["〜もかまわず","without caring about; regardless of; paying no attention to","彼女は人目もかまわず、駅のホームで大声で泣いた。","She cried out loud on the station platform, not caring who was watching.","Doing something without minding what people would normally care about (人目, 周囲, 雨). Often implies disapproval.","बेवास्ता गरेर पनि","Noun + もかまわず / Verb-plain + の + もかまわず","服が汚れるのもかまわず、子どもたちは泥の中で遊び続けた。","The children kept playing in the mud without caring that their clothes were getting dirty.",["manner","criticism"],"","",""],["〜上","from the standpoint of; in terms of; for reasons of","この映画には、教育上好ましくない場面が多い。","This movie has many scenes that are undesirable from an educational standpoint.","Attaches to Sino-Japanese nouns (歴史上, 経験上, 健康上, 表面上). Read じょう, not うえ.","व्यावहारिक/नियमगत दृष्टिले","Noun + 上 / Noun + 上の + Noun","安全上の理由から、この先には立ち入らないでください。","For safety reasons, please do not go beyond this point.",["standpoint","formal","written"],"〜じょう","法律上は問題がなくても、道徳的に許されないこともある。","Even if something is legally fine, it may still be morally unacceptable."],["〜おそれがある","there is a risk that; could (bad outcome)","台風の影響で、今夜から大雨になるおそれがあります。","Due to the typhoon, there is a risk of heavy rain from tonight.","For undesirable possibilities; typical of news, weather reports and official warnings. Also written 〜恐れがある. 〜かねない sounds more like the speaker's own judgment.","नराम्रो घटना हुने जोखिम","Verb-dict + おそれがある / Noun + の + おそれがある","この薬は眠くなるおそれがあるので、服用後の運転は避けてください。","This medicine may cause drowsiness, so avoid driving after taking it.",["possibility","formal"],"","沿岸部には津波のおそれがあるため、避難指示が出された。","An evacuation order was issued for coastal areas because of the risk of a tsunami."],["〜せいか","perhaps because; maybe due to","年のせいか、最近疲れが取れにくくなった。","Maybe it's my age, but lately it takes longer to recover from fatigue.","The speaker isn't sure of the cause. Mostly for bad or neutral results; for good results おかげか is also used.","सायद त्यस कारणले नकारात्मक असर","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / Noun + の + せいか","昨夜遅くまで起きていたせいか、今日は頭がぼんやりしている。","Perhaps because I stayed up late last night, my head feels foggy today.",["reason","conjecture"],"","気のせいか、彼女は少し元気がないように見えた。","Maybe it was just my imagination, but she seemed a little down."],["〜だけあって / 〜だけに","as might be expected (since); precisely because; all the more because","さすが一流ホテルだけあって、サービスが行き届いている。","As you'd expect from a first-class hotel, the service is impeccable.","だけあって praises a result that matches expectations (often with さすが). だけに also means 'all the more because' and can lead to negative outcomes.","त्यही स्तरको अपेक्षा गरिएअनुसार; खास कारणले","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / Noun + だけあって・だけに","十年も日本に住んでいただけあって、彼の日本語はとても自然だ。","As you'd expect from someone who lived in Japan for ten years, his Japanese is very natural.",["reason","emphasis"],"","期待していただけに、落選の知らせはショックだった。","Because I'd had such high hopes, the news that I wasn't selected hit me all the harder."],["〜だけのことはある","it's no wonder; it lives up to; as expected of","この料理は本当においしい。人気店だけのことはある。","This food is really delicious. No wonder the place is so popular.","Judges a result as fully justified by the effort, price or reputation; often with さすが. Like 〜だけあって, but placed at the end of the sentence.","त्यति परिश्रम वा प्रतिष्ठाको मूल्य हुनु","Verb-plain / i-Adj / na-Adj + な / Noun + だけのことはある","素晴らしい演奏だった。さすが毎日練習しているだけのことはある。","It was a wonderful performance. All that daily practice really shows.",["reason","emphasis"],"","",""],["たとえ〜ても","even if; no matter","たとえ反対されても、自分の夢を諦めるつもりはない。","Even if people oppose me, I have no intention of giving up my dream.","たとえ signals a hypothetical 'even if' in advance and strengthens it. A more written variant is たとえ〜としても.","जे भए पनि; यस्तो भए पनि","たとえ + Verb-te + も / たとえ + i-Adj-ku + ても / たとえ + na-Adj + でも / たとえ + Noun + でも","たとえ小さな会社でも、やりがいのある仕事がしたい。","Even if it's a small company, I want to do rewarding work.",["concession","condition","emphasis"],"","たとえ給料が安くても、好きな仕事なら続けられる。","Even if the pay is low, I can keep at it if it's work I love."],["〜やら〜やら","what with ... and ...; and ... and (among other things)","引っ越しの前は、荷造りやら手続きやらで目が回るほど忙しかった。","Before the move, what with packing and paperwork, I was run off my feet.","Lists a few examples among many, often suggesting chaos or mixed feelings. Frequently followed by で + 大変だ / 忙しい.","यो पनि त्यो पनि; थुप्रै कुरा","Noun + やら + Noun + やら / Verb-dict + やら + Verb-dict + やら / i-Adj + やら + i-Adj + やら","財布をなくして、情けないやら腹が立つやらで、泣きたくなった。","I lost my wallet, and between feeling pathetic and angry, I wanted to cry.",["example","emotion"],"","",""],["〜ずに済む / 〜ないで済む","get by without; not have to; be spared from","友人が車で送ってくれたので、タクシーを使わずに済んだ。","My friend gave me a ride, so I didn't have to take a taxi.","Something unpleasant or costly turned out to be unnecessary. する → せずに済む. Compare Noun + で済む, 'be settled with just ...'.","कुनै काम नगरी नै समाधान हुनु","Verb-nai stem + ずに済む / Verb-nai + で済む","早めに治療を始めたおかげで、手術しないで済んだ。","Thanks to starting treatment early, I didn't need surgery.",["necessity","negation"],"〜ずにすむ / 〜ないですむ","",""],["〜ようによっては","depending on how (one does it)","考えようによっては、今回の失敗はいい教訓になったとも言える。","Depending on how you look at it, you could say this failure taught us a good lesson.","Mostly with 考え, 見, 言い, 使い: the result changes with the way A is done. Often offers a positive reinterpretation.","गर्ने तरिकामा निर्भर गर्दै","Verb-stem + ようによっては","古い家具も、使いようによってはおしゃれなインテリアになる。","Depending on how you use it, even old furniture can become stylish decor.",["condition","manner"],"","",""]],"count":123,"level":"N2","source":"OpenJLPT CC BY-SA 4.0, 123 entries tagged N2; Nepali summaries are project-authored; no official JLPT item list."};
